course: dictionary
lesson: 976
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the words around them show which meaning is needed. Boa is one of those words. Look for clues in the sentence before you decide.
explain: «Pythons, boas and anacondas are the giants of the snake world.» The clues are pythons, anacondas and giants of the snake world. These are all snakes, so boa means a large snake here.
explain: «She wore a feather boa to the party.» The clues are feather and wore round the neck for a party. A feather boa is a long, fluffy scarf, so boa means a scarf in this sentence. Always check: swap your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
fact: Some words have more than one meaning. These are called multiple-meaning words.
fact: «Boa» can mean a large snake that kills its prey by wrapping round it and squeezing.
fact: «Boa» can also mean a long, fluffy scarf made of feathers or fur, as in «a feather boa».
fact: Boas and pythons are constrictors: they squeeze their prey so its blood stops flowing.
fact: Boas give birth to live babies, and they have two small spurs near the tail.
exercise: «Pythons, boas and anacondas are the giants of the snake world.» What is a boa in this sentence? | A dressing-up party | *A snake | A type of bird | A long, fluffy scarf
exercise: Ella wears «a feather boa» to the party. What is a boa here? | A dance step | *A long, fluffy scarf | A kind of lizard | A large snake
exercise: «Boas and anacondas give birth to live babies.» What does boa mean here? | A feather scarf | *A large snake | A party hat | A pet fish
test: «Boas and pythons are constrictors that squeeze prey so its blood stops flowing.» Which meaning of boa is used? | A prize for dressing up | A long, fluffy scarf | A type of dance | *A large snake
test: «The actress wrapped a pink boa round her shoulders for the show.» What does boa mean? | A kind of shoe | *A long, fluffy scarf | A dance move | A large snake
exam: Mia says boa means a scarf in «Boas and pythons are constrictors that squeeze prey.» Who is right? | Neither, because boa has no meaning | Mia is right, because squeeze means to wear | *Mia is wrong, because constrictors and squeeze show that boa means a snake | Mia, because boas are always scarves
